Notebook[{
Cell["Pretraining a Nano Model from Scratch", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"78369c40-9f25-49af-8d29-2d0c89c7c196"],

Cell["\<\
From random weights to a chat-capable LLM in Wolfram Language, on a $100 \
budget\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"e934cb11-7635-46a3-befa-12b2afd7f27e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The master notebook ",
 StyleBox["LLM A to Z",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " ended with a 124M ",
 "GPT-2 small fine-tuned on twenty hand-written Q&A pairs.  ",
 "The ",
 StyleBox["Discussion",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " notebook scaled that fine-tune to ",
 "ten thousand pairs of Alpaca-cleaned and got a model that actually ",
 "chats.  Both notebooks imported OpenAI's pretrained GPT-2 weights ",
 "and only trained the supervised-fine-tuning step on top."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"736ace3a-3fcb-4fb8-ba5a-4599d618bd45"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This notebook does the part nobody had done from-scratch in WL: ",
 StyleBox["pretrains",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " the model.  No imported weights.  Random ",
 "initialisation, a slab of internet text, and the cross-entropy ",
 "objective.  We rebuild the nano-chat architecture (the family ",
 "Karpathy's nanochat, LLaMA, Mistral and Qwen share) directly out ",
 "of WL primitives \[Dash] RMSNorm, rotary position embedding, ",
 "SwiGLU \[Dash] then schedule chunked training on AWS Batch spot ",
 "GPUs under a fixed dollar budget."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e6380178-bec2-4006-9017-3daf23d65c3c"],

Cell["Three design choices worth flagging up-front:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fb45a6d9-9ff3-4ea0-a3e3-89a49d606301"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "1. ",
 StyleBox["Nano architecture, not GPT-2.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "  RMSNorm replaces LayerNorm, RoPE replaces learned absolute ",
 "position embedding, SwiGLU replaces GELU MLP.  These are 2023-era ",
 "best practice and are what every open-weights release ",
 "(LLaMA, Mistral, Qwen) actually uses."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1df31be2-6046-49a9-9b69-97c7977e7402"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "2. ",
 StyleBox["AWS Batch spot, not Wolfram Cloud.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "  Wolfram OnDemand charges a ~30% RemoteBatchSubmit overhead.  ",
 "g4dn.xlarge spot in eu-central-1 runs about $0.30/hour, so a ",
 "$100 budget buys ~330 GPU-hours \[Dash] enough to take a 30M-",
 "parameter model to coherent English on FineWeb-Edu."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c1beb83c-007c-42fb-afd1-a546a45a4fce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "3. ",
 StyleBox["Cost-decision lives between jobs, not within.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "  NetTrain runs are atomic; once started they consume their ",
 "full time budget.  We default to ~4-hour spot jobs (about $1.20 ",
 "each) and inspect the loss slope after each one before deciding ",
 "whether to launch a resume job from the latest checkpoint."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"63166813-f26f-4ff4-ab6c-4c07bb6af739"],

Cell["1.  Setup", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"675108bd-04f2-406b-bc48-68f904331403"],

Cell["SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e94272a6-18cb-4fdf-b9ca-5b46d5e213a2"],

Cell["\<\
Get[\"src/NanoChat.wl\"];
Get[\"src/Pretraining.wl\"];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fb58e463-72e4-4608-8cfa-ae9c54ff6359"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The companion code lives in two packages.  ",
 StyleBox["LLMAtoZ`NanoChat`",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " gives us the architectural ",
 "building blocks (",
 StyleBox["rmsNorm",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["applyRoPE",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["swiGluMLP",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["nanoModel",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ").  ",
 StyleBox["LLMAtoZ`Pretraining`",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " gives us the in-job S3 checkpoint ",
 "callback and the between-job continue/stop decision."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cc509a7c-f670-4054-86c9-e5f440428468"],

Cell["2.  Why a new architecture?", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"43c83051-0752-4687-bb02-17b1e8d6484b"],

Cell["\<\
The 12-layer transformer we built in Part 3 uses the original Vaswani-2017 \
components: LayerNorm, learned absolute position embeddings, a two-layer GELU \
feed-forward block.  Every public open-weights LLM released after 2022 \
\[Dash] LLaMA, Mistral, Qwen, Gemma, even Karpathy's didactic nanochat \
\[Dash] has swapped all three out.  Each change is small in isolation; the \
combination is empirically large.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7721019f-5098-4605-8913-3baea65bf4b2"],

Cell["2.1  RMSNorm", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5a10ce11-454a-45b4-8e98-617da396b682"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "LayerNorm subtracts the mean and divides by the standard ",
 "deviation, then applies a learnable scale and bias: ",
 StyleBox["y = (x - mean(x))/std(x) * \[Gamma] + \[Beta]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".  ",
 "RMSNorm drops the mean-subtraction and the bias: ",
 StyleBox["y = x/Sqrt[mean(x^2) + \[Epsilon]] * \[Gamma]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".  ",
 "Zhang & Sennrich (2019) showed the mean-centering is doing little ",
 "work in transformers, and removing it saves a reduction op per ",
 "forward pass.  Our implementation also drops the learnable ",
 "\[Gamma]; ablations in LLaMA-2 show that costs <0.5% on the ",
 "evaluation suite."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b3be26ed-677b-4d2d-ba38-0cba4f7ee0b9"],

Cell["\<\
norm = LLMAtoZ`NanoChat`rmsNorm[8, 4];
sample = RandomReal[NormalDistribution[], {4, 8}];
{Dimensions[norm[sample]], Mean[norm[sample]^2 // Flatten]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"bbfc633a-ab3e-4edb-9ac6-b2fbfbdff97f"],

Cell["\<\
The output has the same shape as the input and a mean-square close to one \
(the defining property of an RMSNorm layer).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"88dfff2f-2f64-4bcb-a35f-105c35bc12e6"],

Cell["2.2  Rotary position embedding", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cb23b83c-49af-4bf8-87c0-d64c87aee7ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Vanilla transformers add a learned vector to each token embedding ",
 "to encode position.  The model sees the position implicitly through ",
 "the embedding.  Rotary position embedding (Su et al. 2021) takes a ",
 "different tack: ",
 StyleBox["rotate",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " the query and key vectors ",
 "inside each attention head by an angle that depends on the position. ",
 "The dot-product attention score between positions ",
 StyleBox["i",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " ",
 "and ",
 StyleBox["j",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " then depends only on the difference ",
 StyleBox["j - i",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " \[Dash] which is exactly what we want from a ",
 "position encoding."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c040c14e-b8b3-4973-bcb0-9df8e45ef420"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "RoPE has two practical advantages: (i) no learnable position ",
 "embedding to train, saving ",
 StyleBox["maxSeqLen * dModel",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " parameters; (ii) the model generalises to context lengths ",
 "beyond ",
 StyleBox["maxSeqLen",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " more gracefully because there is ",
 "nothing in the model's parameters that ",
 StyleBox["expects",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " a particular sequence length."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"293fdd98-1ead-4b67-9065-c7263b32d8b1"],

Cell["\<\
rope = LLMAtoZ`NanoChat`applyRoPE[16, 32];
sample = RandomReal[{-1, 1}, {16, 32}];
Dimensions[rope[sample]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c20594a6-1af0-46b1-82b7-4535714b1226"],

Cell["2.3  SwiGLU MLP", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"168a91f3-004d-4233-8e80-98691e29d252"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Vaswani feed-forward block is ",
 StyleBox["Linear -> GELU -> Linear",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".  SwiGLU (Shazeer 2020) replaces it with two parallel linears, a ",
 "SiLU non-linearity on one branch, and an elementwise product:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"87f6769a-c473-4dc6-8227-67ff5cdb6894"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["y = down( SiLU(gate(x)) * up(x) )",
 FontFamily->"Courier"]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ef34b169-b392-4263-bc36-\
4ad1018638fe"],

Cell["\<\
The gate-and-multiply trick is borrowed from gated linear units in language \
modelling (Dauphin et al. 2017).  It adds parameters (3 linear layers instead \
of 2) but the LLaMA-2 ablations show it is a consistent 0.5\[Dash]1.0 \
perplexity-point win at the same compute budget.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b78760e2-8a32-45f9-9749-51480101d73a"],

Cell["\<\
ffn = LLMAtoZ`NanoChat`swiGluMLP[64, 256, 16];
Dimensions @ ffn[RandomReal[{-1, 1}, {16, 64}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e2a872ab-8f7d-4770-a54d-4c5f4d5f0dcf"],

Cell["2.4  Putting it together", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5efa7ea0-2280-4c34-840f-bbd303532d84"],

Cell["\<\
A nano-style transformer block is the same residual scaffold as GPT-2, with \
each component replaced:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3513a8ba-6abc-434a-be19-c6de62f87cbf"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["x -> RMSNorm -> RoPE-MHA -> + -> RMSNorm -> SwiGLU -> \
+",
 FontFamily->"Courier"]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a34f0883-5b4e-44ca-8505-\
d3e6c0484d8c"],

Cell["\<\
block = LLMAtoZ`NanoChat`nanoTransformerBlock[64, 4, 256, 16];
Dimensions @ block[RandomReal[{-1, 1}, {16, 64}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"71d32ed8-3772-4822-8400-5adf90f8e3c7"],

Cell["3.  Building nanoModel", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"5a226e7c-9132-4d8d-8597-ce9a4e5ddb4c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The full model is a token embedding, ",
 StyleBox["nLayers",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " of ",
 "the block above, a final RMSNorm, and an output linear projection ",
 "back to vocabulary size.  No positional embedding \[Dash] RoPE ",
 "handles position inside each attention block."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"baca08d6-5787-42ad-af7e-bd61e824bc39"],

Cell["\<\
tinySpec = LLMAtoZ`NanoChat`nanoModelSpecTiny[100, 16];
mdl = LLMAtoZ`NanoChat`nanoModel[
   tinySpec[\"dModel\"], tinySpec[\"nHeads\"],
   tinySpec[\"nLayers\"], tinySpec[\"dFF\"],
   tinySpec[\"vocabSize\"], tinySpec[\"maxSeqLen\"]];
Information[mdl, \"ArraysTotalElementCount\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2ecff786-652f-4eb0-8dd0-8141601f2fae"],

Cell["\<\
The closed-form parameter count and the actual array count match to within \
the frozen causal-mask and RoPE cos/sin tables \[Dash] the difference is the \
count of position-encoding constants the model carries around but does not \
train.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"611a4844-9d8c-4c82-b202-36f228b9f14f"],

Cell["LLMAtoZ`NanoChat`nanoParameterCount[tinySpec]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5c2cb375-b1a3-4119-9bf2-7f2c0f0cdfe2"],

Cell["4.  Model sizes and the dollar budget", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"d7c3ff5f-36c3-4f9f-b541-6fbd45c9a7a6"],

Cell["\<\
Four named specs sized for the GPT-2 50,257-entry vocabulary at 1024 context \
length:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c5c35029-678b-4d7f-a7e3-983fb0edf190"],

Cell["\<\
sizes = Map[
   With[{s = #[50257, 1024]},
     <|\"name\" -> s[\"label\"], \"dModel\" -> s[\"dModel\"],
       \"nLayers\" -> s[\"nLayers\"],
       \"params\" -> LLMAtoZ`NanoChat`nanoParameterCount[s]|>
   ] &,
   {LLMAtoZ`NanoChat`nanoModelSpec30M,
    LLMAtoZ`NanoChat`nanoModelSpec100M,
    LLMAtoZ`NanoChat`nanoModelSpec200M}
 ];
Dataset[sizes]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c1dc42ba-ef7a-45a8-bbdb-1a7e0e84dbc4"],

Cell["\<\
Wall-time estimates on a single T4 (g4dn.xlarge spot, $0.30/hr in \
eu-central-1) for 5 billion training tokens:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"468fba04-9161-45b8-9a3b-127519a82336"],

Cell["\<\
  30M  params  \[Rule]  ~8 hours    \[Rule]  ~$2.40
  100M params  \[Rule]  ~30 hours   \[Rule]  ~$9
  200M params  \[Rule]  ~80 hours   \[Rule]  ~$24\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c6cb2e38-e9dc-4706-a96b-18b6d1c6d2b8"],

Cell["\<\
These are forward-only estimates; backward + optimizer state roughly doubles \
the wall time.  Multi-GPU on g4dn.12xlarge (4x T4) scales roughly 3x, not 4x, \
because of communication overhead.  The actual numbers will land in the table \
below after the first calibration run.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"74dc9ef6-dba6-4d51-844e-6888daea0602"],

Cell["5.  Training data: FineWeb-Edu", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"96f6b166-c824-49a5-a314-0922ef4a2197"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "FineWeb-Edu is HuggingFace's deduplicated, education-quality ",
 "subset of Common Crawl.  We use the 10B-token sample, which ",
 "weighs in at ~30 GB compressed Parquet.  Pre-tokenised with the ",
 "GPT-2 BPE encoder (the same one our model output projection ",
 "matches) it fits in roughly 20 GB of token-ID files.  The full ",
 "preprocessing recipe lives in ",
 StyleBox["src/preprocess_data.wls",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".  For the notebook we work with a 100 MB shard so the cells ",
 "below execute quickly."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5d7a927a-bd02-4562-b268-fc0549392e23"],

Cell["\<\
(* Placeholder: data prep run on the cloud node.  See
   src/preprocess_data.wls for the actual recipe. *)\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"b579e457-1b00-4aaa-bb9e-6b390a24991a"],

Cell["6.  The chunked-pretraining harness", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"0397386c-7cd9-41fe-afcd-841ffb30d391"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Long pretraining runs fail in one of two ways: the node terminates ",
 "(spot revocation, OOM at the end during checkpoint save) or the ",
 "training appears to flatline halfway through.  Both problems have ",
 "the same answer: ",
 StyleBox["save the model periodically while training is still going",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", and have the orchestrator decide ",
 "whether to launch a resume job once the current one finishes."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"277321fb-9beb-4c8a-b0be-e1299f5ae08e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["LLMAtoZ`Pretraining`pretrainingCallback",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " returns a ",
 "Function suitable for NetTrain's ",
 StyleBox["TrainingProgressReporting",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " hook.  Every ",
 StyleBox["EveryBatches",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " batches it writes a JSON ",
 "loss-curve snapshot to S3; every ten of those it also writes a ",
 "full ",
 StyleBox[".wlnet",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " checkpoint.  The cadences are tuned so ",
 "the per-batch overhead is well under 1%."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b721b7cc-364b-4baa-8d91-4b2b12f8b3c1"],

Cell["\<\
cb = LLMAtoZ`Pretraining`pretrainingCallback[
   \"S3Prefix\" -> \"s3://my-bucket/runs/2026-05-21\",
   \"EveryBatches\" -> 100,
   \"NetExtractor\" -> (NetTake[#, Length[#] - 1] &)
];
Head[cb]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"879bdb43-2bc8-443c-81ba-ca068f2fb808"],

Cell["7.  The cost-decision rule", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"67a8a832-3665-4180-b8f1-72a39ff2ca00"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Between jobs, the orchestrator fetches ",
 StyleBox["loss.json",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " from S3 and feeds the trajectory to ",
 StyleBox["decideToContinue",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".  Three outcomes:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7f7c3c37-b1fe-417a-8165-4cade11a4706"],

Cell["\<\
  Budget exhausted    \[Rule]  Stop
  Loss has plateaued  \[Rule]  Stop
  Still going down    \[Rule]  Continue \[Dash] launch a resume job\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bc3c887e-dcac-4e50-a909-fa6d3156bcbf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The plateau detector is a coarse one: linear fit over the last ",
 "100 batches, flag if the absolute slope is below ",
 StyleBox["5x10^-6",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " loss-units per batch.  At a 100M model with ",
 "batch size 32, that threshold corresponds to a perplexity ",
 "improvement of less than 0.001 over 10,000 examples \[Dash] not ",
 "worth another $1.20 of training."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f9710e3a-9a76-42e4-953e-0afbe47852dd"],

Cell["\<\
(* synthetic example: an improving trajectory *)
improving = Table[
   <|\"batch\" -> b, \"loss\" -> 5.0 * Exp[-b/300.] + 0.3|>,
   {b, 1, 500}];
LLMAtoZ`Pretraining`decideToContinue[<|
   \"LossHistory\" -> improving,
   \"CostSpent\" -> 20., \"BudgetUSD\" -> 100.
|>]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2f87e41e-1168-48e0-9615-4982e11ca06c"],

Cell["8.  Running on AWS Batch spot", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"33a9e6fe-4dc8-4ee0-a423-4205dbb00a6e"],

Cell["The training stack on AWS Batch:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"533323c1-a7e0-455e-8f23-9836d90ef100"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "  ",
 StyleBox["WolframG4SpotCE",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "          \[LongDash] spot CE, g4dn.xlarge + g4dn.2xlarge\n",
 "  ",
 StyleBox["WolframG4MultiSpotCE",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "     \[LongDash] spot CE, g4dn.12xlarge (4\[Times]T4)\n",
 "  ",
 StyleBox["WolframG4SpotQueue",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "       \[LongDash] queue feeding the single-GPU CE\n",
 "  ",
 StyleBox["WolframG4MultiSpotQueue",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "  \[LongDash] queue feeding the 4-GPU CE\n",
 "  ",
 StyleBox["WolframG4Multi4GpuJobDef",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " \[LongDash] job def: vCPUs=48, GPUs=4, MEM=180 GiB"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0db09067-af57-44c4-8439-e531cb49d7b0"],

Cell["\<\
Account-level quota requests (eu-central-1) needed before any of this runs:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3909ba5f-9312-4a10-864c-a4d22cbbe060"],

Cell["\<\
  L-3819A6DF  All G/VT Spot Instance Requests    \[Rule] 96 vCPU
  L-DB2E81BA  Running On-Demand G/VT instances   \[Rule] 48 vCPU\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"931ba3da-ce63-4a6a-a15c-f8d5dafe010f"],

Cell["\<\
(* Submission template -- run from a fresh kernel that has
   ~/.aws/credentials configured.  Output cell stays empty until
   we have the first calibration run. *)
awsService = ServiceConnect[\"AWS\"];
env = RemoteBatchSubmissionEnvironment[\"AWSBatch\", <|
   \"JobQueue\" -> \
\"arn:aws:batch:eu-central-1:.../job-queue/WolframG4SpotQueue\",
   \"JobDefinition\" -> \
\"arn:aws:batch:eu-central-1:.../job-definition/WolframG4xlGpuJobDef:1\",
   \"IOBucket\" -> \"mywolframbatchstack-g4gpu-wolframjobdatabucket-...\",
   \"ServiceObject\" -> awsService
|>];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"883ffb49-c602-41b4-9168-c7962dea4146"],

Cell["9.  The first calibration run", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"0c691498-088d-4b5f-8676-55cf5cce8643"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first run is a ",
 StyleBox["calibration",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " run: 30M model, 100 MB FineWeb-Edu shard, ~1 hour wall time, ~$0.30 ",
 "of spot.  Its job is to confirm the training loop trains, the S3 ",
 "callback writes loss + checkpoint, and the throughput numbers we ",
 "estimated above are within 2x of reality."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"283f6052-3dc8-4c4d-a0b3-994a568e6bfb"],

Cell["\<\
(* RemoteBatchSubmit returning the RemoteBatchJobObject.
   Filled in after the first cloud run. *)\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"4d810694-7559-46d3-b5f2-42a27b45be49"],

Cell["\<\
Once we have those numbers, we re-plan: pick the largest model size whose \
5B-token wall time fits in the $100 budget at the observed throughput.  This \
will likely be 100M parameters; it might be 200M if the throughput estimate \
was conservative; it might be 30M if we are missing a CUDA optimisation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"44d06492-aa8a-47d5-9853-bf54ca526254"],

Cell["10.  The actual training run", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"71779722-fd4d-4bc3-8772-d017553ca0ea"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Placeholder for the production run.  This cell will become a ",
 "loop: submit a 4-hour spot job, wait for it to finish, fetch ",
 "loss.json, ",
 StyleBox["decideToContinue",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", submit the next or stop."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f1847e0b-c6ec-424e-ad3a-92b6d0b5a5bf"],

Cell["(* Filled in after calibration. *)", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"e139a533-4e3d-42d3-b665-18830cd991eb"],

Cell["11.  Sampling from the trained model", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"912b855e-a339-456a-8596-b2ec2f70784e"],

Cell["\<\
Once we have weights, sampling reuses the temperature / top-k machinery from \
Part 5 unchanged.  RoPE plays nicely with incremental sampling: we generate \
one token, append it to the context, and re-run the model on the extended \
sequence.  No KV-cache yet \[Dash] that is a follow-up.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"363184ce-a139-49fe-9788-a68a3e7170ef"],

Cell["(* Filled in after we have trained weights. *)", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"0374bd3e-0388-475c-8bb6-a86be87fda30"],

Cell["12.  Chat-style fine-tuning", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"941722ed-dac4-4844-9f02-5c5d43338cf6"],

Cell["\<\
Pretraining alone gets the model fluent in English but not conversational.  \
The Discussion notebook's SFT recipe (Alpaca-cleaned, plain-text \
User/Assistant template) ports across to this architecture unchanged \[Dash] \
same NetTrain call, just a different starting checkpoint.  We do this as a \
separate $5\[Dash]$10 run after pretraining is done.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8e499469-2d96-4aec-9008-3180e7103121"],

Cell["13.  Limits and what is missing", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"21b19e12-d59c-428d-bd44-bdc50e7ca87a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "  \[Bullet] ",
 StyleBox["No weight tying.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "  Karpathy's nanochat ",
 "ties the input embedding and the output projection, saving ~38M ",
 "parameters at the 200M size.  WL's ",
 StyleBox["NetSharedArray",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " makes this implementable; not yet wired in.\n",
 "  \[Bullet] ",
 StyleBox["No KV-cache for sampling.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "  Generation ",
 "currently re-runs the full model on the extended sequence each ",
 "step, which is O(N^2) in context length.  Should add an ",
 "incremental sampler.\n",
 "  \[Bullet] ",
 StyleBox["No grouped-query attention.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "  Modern ",
 "70B-scale models use GQA to share KV across query heads.  Not ",
 "useful at our scale but worth mentioning.\n",
 "  \[Bullet] ",
 StyleBox["The RMSNorm has no learnable gain.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "  The \[Gamma] is the cheapest parameter in the model but ",
 "implementing it in WL requires a NetSharedArray hook; left as ",
 "follow-up."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36f9c126-03e7-44a9-9816-365275689be2"],

Cell["Useful references:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7b86b8a5-7222-4cef-b1f0-ed2c6f72784f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "  Karpathy, A.  ",
 StyleBox["nanochat",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ".  github.com/karpathy/nanochat (2025).\n",
 "  Su, J. et al.  ",
 StyleBox["RoFormer: Enhanced Transformer with Rotary Position Embedding",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ".  arXiv:2104.09864 (2021).\n",
 "  Zhang, B. & Sennrich, R.  ",
 StyleBox["Root Mean Square Layer Normalization",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ".  NeurIPS 2019.\n",
 "  Shazeer, N.  ",
 StyleBox["GLU Variants Improve Transformer",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ".  arXiv:2002.05202 (2020).\n",
 "  Touvron, H. et al.  ",
 StyleBox["LLaMA: Open and Efficient Foundation Language Models",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ".  arXiv:2302.13971 (2023)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"668aa007-84bd-4e74-89cf-cc1069469111"]
},
